    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d69">

                <pb facs="0157" n="77" xml:id="pg77"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A5/689: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chairman of the American Delegation</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>)<anchor n="62" xml:id="d69-f1"
                    />
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-02-27T18:00:00-05:00">February 27,
                            1936—6 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>48. Your 110, February 27, noon. With regard to your alternatives based on the
                    possibility that the Italians will not now join in a naval agreement, our views
                    would be as follows:</p>
                <p>Your first alternative. We would be willing to enter into an agreement with
                    England and France with the appropriate safeguard clauses. As far as the manner
                    of German adherence is concerned, we refer you to our 47, February 26, 8
                    p.m.</p>
                <p>Your second alternative. We prefer to follow the procedure outlined in our 46,
                    February 25, 8 p.m. It might be misunderstood here if we assumed the position of
                    joint inviting power with the British for obtaining the adherences of other
                    countries to the naval treaty, particularly in view of the political atmosphere
                    now prevailing on the continent.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
